title: Migrate relay installations to private fail-closed reachability
updated_at: "2026-07-21T13:50:18Z"
---
## Purpose

Ship a safe operator/user migration from current global authenticated-peer discovery and default-allow inbound policy to private, consent-gated reachability.

## Work

- Define upgrade behaviour for existing registrations, outboxes, inboxes, policies, address books, pins, managed sessions, and remote aliases.
- Default production to fail closed after the approved compatibility boundary; never silently preserve unsolicited first-contact reachability.
- Provide explicit commands/configuration to issue/share/revoke/rotate contact routes and to audit current exposure without printing reusable secrets accidentally.
- Make development bypasses explicit, noisy, and excluded from production security claims.
- Update doctor/health diagnostics to detect legacy default-allow, missing migration, insecure endpoint schemes, stale grants, and mixed-version downgrade risk.
- Document operational recovery and rollback without weakening the invariant.

## Acceptance evidence

- Upgrade tests cover old state, mixed versions, interrupted migration, retry, rollback, and idempotence.
- CLI/help/doctor output is tested and does not leak capabilities.
- A production deployment cannot report healthy while retaining unintended global discovery/default-allow admission.